The routing skill (skills/routing/SKILL.md) began as a rewrite of the skill in
claude-model-router by Rajvardhman (https://github.com/Rajvardhman05/claude-model-router),
which is itself a condensation of Anthropic's model-selection guidance. That
project is MIT licensed:

    MIT License
    Copyright (c) 2026 Rajvardhman

The idea of routing by delegation rather than switching the session model,
the escalation order (verify, then effort, then model) and the shape of the
routing table come from it. Where gearshift's table differs, docs/HOW_IT_WORKS.md
says why and cites the measurement.

Measurements quoted in this repository are Anthropic's, from its public
documentation, and are cited where they appear. gearshift is an independent
project and is not affiliated with or endorsed by Anthropic.
